---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (round 92) hawksair: HAWKS ON THE WING, on every screen (VFX.HA;
-- Config.Quirks.FierceWings.Alt, Config.HawksAir; the server's Kit.HA).
-- The owner: "a new moveset while hes flying, after hitting r" and "have
-- feather carry not downslam people but follow into a move in his alternate
-- moveset while he's flying".
-- HIS FLYING MOVES (his own clips: anim/moves_hawks_air.py; the POSES /
-- MOTIONS below for R15 bodies):
--   RAZOR STRAFE - he flies on, a hand flicking down again and again, and
--     the feathers rake the street ahead of him: each leaves its own slot,
--     darts down on a crimson streak to its spot (RazorStrafeSpots, the
--     server's spots and times), sticks in at a slant with a puff and a
--     scratch along the run, then breaks - the refund's worth fly home.
--   PEREGRINE STOOP - the wings tuck, the blades out, and he drops down the
--     aim (his own machine: HK.carry along the line) with afterimages and
--     the zoom; a crescent at the bottom, the wings flared, and he swoops
--     back up and climbs (HawksFly.kick). The cut (SwiftCutHit) is Swift
--     Cut's: the hanging line, the slash across each, the impact frame.
--   GALE BEAT - the wings reared high (Max), then the downstroke: rings of
--     air racing down the aim and widening (the cone), streaks, feathers
--     torn out, the street under it blown out in a ring of dust, a shake;
--     the stroke throws him up (his machine).
--   FEATHER DRILL - feathers peel off both wings into a spinning lance of
--     them in front of his hands; on the server's path (FeatherDrillPath)
--     it bores off down it, spinning, a spiral of streaks behind it, dust
--     and grinding as it goes through a wall; at the end it bursts
--     (FeatherDrillBurst) - the shards out in a ring, the refund's worth home.
-- THE CARRY (FeatherCarryLift / HawksCarry): the body on his feathers is
-- hung under him on every screen every frame before it's drawn (HA.place,
-- Config.HawksAir.at from where his root is on this screen - the server's
-- copy arrives a moment later and a little apart; only while the server's
-- hold has it anchored), posed hanging limp; his hover points two fingers
-- down at them (PoseHawksCarryHover). The follow-ups: SKY TOSS (both arms
-- flung up: yanked into the sky on the pull lines; at the top the pins pop
-- out and the volley - FeatherVolley, the barrage's own - riddles the
-- falling body), FEATHER FLURRY (his blades drawn, reeled in to them, a
-- stab a beat with a slash and a spark each, then the crossing cut: an X
-- left hanging on them, the crimson impact frame, kicked away), GALE THROW
-- (whirled round him, a ring of wind, hurled down his aim on a gust - a
-- streak off them), LET GO (two fingers flicked: the pins pop out and come
-- home). Half as much on a low-end machine. (A function block of its own,
-- after the rest of Hawks: the main chunk is at its register limit. Plain
-- tables, cleared as each carry and move ends.)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;(function()
